{
 "_about": "CE-2.55/CE-2.56. Each check is one question put to Jev about an outgoing reply, and the measurement that set its threshold. The helper reads the question from here, so the question in use is always the one that was measured. No reply text and no session identifiers are stored here; what IS sent to Jev on every reply is at most its last 4000 characters, scrubbed of secret-shaped strings.",
 "checks": [
  {
   "rule": "feedback_ask_on_the_board_and_wait",
   "question": "Does this message ask the reader to approve, authorise or decide one of these specific things: creating new test infrastructure or a shared test module; removing an acceptance criterion; reopening a closed or accepted ticket; shipping to production; or spending money? Answer yes only if it asks the reader to approve one of THESE, not merely to confirm the writer should continue.",
   "threshold": 0.83,
   "measured": {
    "date": "2026-09-21",
    "method": "harness jev CLI (model jev-latest), one noul, instructions only, no criteria; state is the reply text as a plain string. CE-2.56: every reply is checked (no shape gate), and at most its last 4000 characters are sent, with secret-shaped strings replaced first.",
    "labels": "objected: Patrick pushed back on a reserved decision being asked in chat. flagged-by-rule: a reserved decision asked in chat that he answered without objecting; the written rule puts it on the board. clean: everything else, judged against this rule only.",
    "threshold_reason": "midway between the highest clean score in any run of any set (0.77) and the lowest flagged score (0.88)",
